---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import FeatureTable from '../components/FeatureTable.astro'
import MilestoneList from '../components/MilestoneList.astro'
import { href } from '../lib/url'
---
<SiteLayout title="Roadmap" path="roadmap" description="Nova's evidence-backed feature status and milestone roadmap.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Living document · updated with evidence</span>
      <h1>Roadmap, not theater.</h1>
      <p>This matrix is generated from the same maturity manifest used by the documentation. Tested means automated tests pass; planned means it is not implemented.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 style="font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 16px;">Milestones A–I</h2>
      <MilestoneList />
      <p class="notice"><strong>Milestone B is partial.</strong> Electron is retained with a scored decision, but Tauri and native-shell spikes were not built. Milestone I is active: the public repository is live and the Pages deployment is verified at <a href="https://jd4rider.github.io/nova/">jd4rider.github.io/nova</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><div><div class="kicker">Central status manifest</div><h2>Feature ledger</h2></div><a class="button" href={href('status/')}>Open status page</a></div>
      <div class="card" style="padding: 8px 18px; overflow-x: auto;"><FeatureTable /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-3">
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon">1</div><h3>Next: GUI proof</h3><p>Add Playwright Electron smoke coverage: open workspace, edit, save, diagnostics, build/run and terminal.</p><div class="meta">Milestone E/G</div></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon">2</div><h3>Language depth</h3><p>Incremental LSP sync, generic structs/enums/methods, `dyn Trait` dispatch, mutable captures and a Nova wasm backend — each with tests and docs.</p><div class="meta">Milestone F/G</div></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon">3</div><h3>Release evidence</h3><p>Unsigned macOS DMG, Windows EXE and brew tap are published. Next: signing/notarization, Windows launch verification, Intel/Linux installers and benchmarks.</p><div class="meta">Milestone H/I</div></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
